  "scope": "One original nonblocking shared-Queue Graph submission owns its exact proxy, Queue and whole terminal contract once. Independent fixed caller-owned I32 output views compose into one atomic consumer bundle. Six finite CUDA component cases; no pending Store/KV ticket or model pipeline.",
  "implementation": {
    "api": [
      "detail::SubmissionSource::create(Invocation&, Completion&& exact_proxy, const StorageOwner& metadata_owner)",
      "SubmissionSource::poll/wait observe the one original Completion under one ordinary mutex",
      "SubmissionSource::detach explicitly closes export and returns the original producer pin only after all view borrows end and actual producer retirement",
      "detail::OutputSource::create(const SubmissionSource&, ValueId output, const StorageOwner&, const LeasePool&)",
      "OutputSource::detach preserves a real original ready ReadLease only after whole success AND actual retirement",
      "bind_outputs/prepare_outputs/submit_outputs(Invocation&, span<const OutputBinding>, ...)",
      "ReplayAccess::can_reuse_capture(const Invocation&, span<const ReplayInputBinding>) checks the complete final replacement tuple"
    ],
    "facts": [
      "The old OutputSource::create Completion argument and the old three singular output adapters are removed, without compatibility overloads. Public Invocation/Completion layouts, provider runtime facts and ReplayOptions are unchanged.",
      "SubmissionSource keeps one exact original RetainedCompletion proxy, one actual Queue and one results pin; typed views do not move or observe separate Completions. A separate existing CompletionRetention node keeps metadata StorageOwner through true native retirement without a source/Completion self-cycle.",
      "Each typed view separately validates its original published value, dense I32 description, exact full original writer, real LeasePool domain, compiled StorageDomain resource owner, allocator lifetime and same actual Context. No whole-pool read permission or pending ReadLease is invented.",
      "One binding bundle strongly retains every typed view and its actual storage owner. Each InputSource attachment uses the same immutable SubmissionSource identity, so original dependency dedup does not lose the second view or create a second status observer.",
      "Atomic InputAccess::bind validates the complete incoming bundle before committing original bindings. View identities/pending authority markers change only after successful commit. Exact adapter matching checks both source identity and the actual retained bundle state; dedup still uses original (vtable, identity).",
      "Distinct consumer inputs are required. Readonly fanout from the same source value is allowed by the API, with real per-entry lease admission. That extra fanout variant was not independently executed in this finite window.",
      "Ordinary Invocation::submit cannot bypass the missing pending-read authority. Original OrderedGraphSubmission admits each actual lease and InputSources reconciles the full original producer status after consumer retirement.",
      "Capture-only qualification checks all replacement inputs together against existing full physical records. Missing artifacts/alias proof or tuple changes cannot record pending values or fall back to managed Commands.",
      "poll/wait do not implicitly close export, even when no views exist. OutputSource::detach only makes its own permission independent. Explicit SubmissionSource::detach returns a control-operation status: a failed-but-actually-retired submission can close successfully, while its poll/wait still report the original mathematical error.",
      "Borrow/ref teardown uses the common ordinary mutex only for borrowed pointers/counts, then destroys retained view/common refs outside that lock. Local StorageOwners cover allocator deallocation and original producer release. The original compiled domain retains its actual output resource through eventual allocation destruction."
    ]
  },
