    "assertions": [
      "An actual CUDA host gate proves the original producer and consumer are pending, with watchdog release on all exits. The pending I32->checked Gather chain uses the original Queue and original lease domains.",
      "A genuine selected Store region exercises its existing metadata-only prepare/seal hooks while consuming the pending token, then take returns its original actual writer after retirement.",
      "A controlled original checked-index error prevents consumer publication. Typed detach preserves that error; after true retirement and release of borrowed views, common detach returns Ok, original outcome_available is true, and common wait still has exactly the original error code/message. This is not a native/driver fault injection.",
      "After successful view detach followed by explicit common detach, the producer can bind another genuine writer and submit a new generation while the original consumer is still gated. The old source remains immutable and preserves its old terminal verdict.",
      "A native Gather+Add consumer legally reuses its real existing capture: recorded count zero, reused count one, one source wait and zero host waits. Physical tuple misses reject and preserve the original recording; managed producer support is not claimed.",
      "The new producer has two real independent I32 output writers at different original offsets; the consumer has two checked Gather inputs. A late foreign-input bundle rejects without replacing the first old ready input or claiming either view. The complete retry succeeds.",
      "The two-value bundle reports source_count=1, device_wait_count=1 and host_wait_count=0, while both outputs retain independent resource proofs. Final values are [30,31] and [20,21], actual native uses return to zero and final release returns all output blocks."
    ]
